        <mxCell id="rules" parent="1" style="rounded=1;arcSize=3;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFF8E6;strokeColor=#D9A13B;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#1A1A1A;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingRight=8;spacingTop=6;spacingBottom=6;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono;fontSource=https%3A%2F%2Ffonts.googleapis.com%2Fcss%3Ffamily%3DJetBrains%2BMono;" value="&lt;b&gt;Rules&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Breaking&lt;/b&gt; = removing / renaming a field or endpoint, tightening validation, changing a type or meaning, a new required input, reusing a proto field number, removing an enum value. Additive changes stay in the same version.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Deprecation:&lt;/b&gt; &lt;code&gt;Deprecation: true&lt;/code&gt; + &lt;code&gt;Sunset: &amp;lt;date&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; + &lt;code&gt;Link: rel=&quot;successor-version&quot;&lt;/code&gt; on every old-version response; portal banner and e-mail to subscribers; minimum 6 months (12 months for partner product).&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Retire:&lt;/b&gt; only when usage is zero or the Sunset date has passed with notice; old version then returns 410 Gone with a Problem Details link to the guide.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;GraphQL:&lt;/b&gt; fields marked @deprecated(reason) and kept until persisted-query usage drops to zero · &lt;b&gt;events:&lt;/b&gt; dual-publish v1 + v2 · &lt;b&gt;gRPC:&lt;/b&gt; new package version pos.x.v2, old one served side by side.&lt;br&gt;• (C) = re-check the old version&#39;s usage every month" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="112" width="1960" x="40" y="790" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
